WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:04.750
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.350
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.410
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.610
Hello, everyone.

9
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:26.970
Good morning.

10
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:28.810
Or afternoon.

11
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:29.550
Or evening.

12
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:30.790
Or evening, whenever you listen.

13
00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.830
When will I stop saying good morning?

14
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:34.850
I like it.

15
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.010
I think you should never stop.

16
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:36.450
Okay.

17
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.950
Today's episode is Test the Store.

18
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:45.830
It was Season 8, Episode 17, written by Mindy Kaling and directed by Brent Forrester.

19
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:52.330
I love it every time I see directed by Brent Forrester because I know we're going to get some fun nugget.

20
00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.710
Oh, and we have some.

21
00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.070
Yeah.

22
00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:55.910
It's very exciting.

23
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.530
Here's your summary for today.

24
00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:06.550
Today, the Tallahassee team hosts the test launch of the new Sabre store, and it does not quite go as planned.

25
00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:07.190
Mm-mm.

26
00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.530
That's an understatement.

27
00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:08.990
Mm-hmm.

28
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:16.130
Meanwhile, Andy saves Pam from being attacked in the parking lot, resulting in a self-defense class taught by Toby.

29
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.330
How excited was Toby?

30
00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.230
Anytime we need him for anything.

31
00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:21.870
Anything.

32
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.370
But, I mean, he was like, let me go change my clothes.

33
00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:26.770
Let me go get my cup.

34
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:27.110
Yeah.

35
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:27.990
Oh, my cup.

36
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:28.710
That's right.

37
00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.350
All right.

38
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.630
Fast fact number one, guest star Tig Notaro.

39
00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:35.410
Yeah.

40
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:36.810
We got fan mail.

41
00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.010
Alexis K.

42
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.470
from California said,

43
00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.470
Tig Notaro is so incredible.

44
00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:49.390
This episode was the first thing I ever saw her in, and then my husband and I stumbled on one of her Netflix specials, and we have been big fans ever since.

45
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.510
I'd love to know everything about her casting for this role.

46
00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.010
I know she and Ed Helms were friends, but was there any other story about her casting?

47
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:02.450
I wish she'd had a bigger guest role because she's so funny and her deadpan humor is perfect for The Office.

48
00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.710
I did, too.

49
00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.590
I really thought maybe her character was going to come back.

50
00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:07.390
Me, too.

51
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.450
Maybe in the parking lot at the end of the day.

52
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:09.810
Yeah.

53
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.970
I so thought that because just the way she's like, you guys do great work.

54
00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:14.530
Yeah.

55
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:15.690
I love your paper.

56
00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:16.410
Love your paper.

57
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.530
I was like, I wonder if she's going to come back.

58
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:29.230
Well, everyone, Tig is a stand-up comedian who had been on the Sarah Silverman program before being on The Office, and Mindy was a huge fan of hers.

59
00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:36.490
You know, Mindy wrote this episode, and she requested Tig for the role of the mom, and that's how we got Tig on the show.

60
00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:37.550
We were so lucky.

61
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:44.610
Now, I'm not sure if everyone knows, but about a year after Tig worked on the show, she was diagnosed with stage 2 breast cancer,

62
00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:51.550
and she did this stand-up show at Largo just days after getting her cancer diagnosis.

63
00:02:51.550 --> 00:03:01.450
Ed Helms, who had known her from the stand-up world, had the set right before her, and, you know, the comedian who goes before introduces the next comedian.

64
00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:01.810
Mm-hmm.

65
00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:11.990
So Ed Helms introduced her, introduced this now legendary comedy set where she just immediately starts talking about having cancer.

66
00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.790
So earnestly.

67
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:14.590
Yes.

68
00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.150
No, I have cancer.

69
00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.550
It takes you back at first, and then you're on this ride with her.

70
00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:20.910
I don't even know how to describe it.

71
00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:27.230
Ed told me that he was standing backstage with the other comedians, and no one knew that this was going to be her set.

72
00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:27.850
Wow.

73
00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:31.650
And he said, you just watched something historic happen.

74
00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.670
I actually have a clip of the beginning.

75
00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:34.770
Oh, okay.

76
00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:49.500
I am now very thrilled, and it is my great privilege to bring to the stage someone who is extremely nice, extremely funny, extremely warm-hearted, and wonderful,

77
00:03:49.500 --> 00:04:01.400
and also was on The Office once, and is a very, very dear friend who I love and cherish, and you do, too, of course.

78
00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.860
I'm talking about Tig Notaro.

79
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:03.640
Hello.

80
00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.030
Good evening.

81
00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.530
Hello.

82
00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.420
I have cancer.

83
00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.240
How are you?

84
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.120
Hi.

85
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:22.840
How are you?

86
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.080
Is everybody having a good time?

87
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.240
I have cancer.

88
00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:26.940
How are you?

89
00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:28.960
Ah.

90
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.300
It's a good time.

91
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.540
Diagnosed with cancer.

92
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:35.550
Ah.

93
00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:36.870
Feels good.

94
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.810
Just diagnosed with cancer.

95
00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.930
Oh, God.

96
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.920
Oh, my God.

97
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:59.640
It's weird, because with humor, the equation is tragedy plus time equals comedy.

98
00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:10.210
I am just at tragedy right now.

99
00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.750
That's just where I am in the equation.

100
00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:22.390
So, guys, I was trading texts with Ed Helms about this, and he reminded me that This American Life did a podcast where they interviewed Tig about this comedy set.

101
00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:29.970
They play a big portion of the comedy set, and I started listening to it while I was driving home from physical therapy the other day,

102
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:36.450
and I ended up sitting in my driveway in my parked car just laughing and sobbing.

103
00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.330
I'm getting emotional just thinking about it.

104
00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:44.490
It is an absolute revelation, because not only did she just find out that she had stage 2 cancer,

105
00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:49.750
she had also just gotten out of the hospital after having this horrible bacterial infection.

106
00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:57.690
Her mother had just died in a terrible accident, and she had just broken up with her girlfriend, like, all in the past few months.

107
00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:07.370
And she does a comedy set about all of that, and you're just like, I don't even know how I'm laughing, but I'm also crying.

108
00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.130
I highly recommend it.

109
00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.730
You should definitely check it out.

110
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:16.250
I want to hear her on This American Life, because I heard that set a long time ago.

111
00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:24.710
But I'd be curious to hear her now talk about doing it, and what that process was like for her.

112
00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.190
Like, was it healing?

113
00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.890
What was her motivation?

114
00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.950
So I really want to hear that.

115
00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.450
Yeah, she does talk about that.

116
00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.530
I won't ruin it for anyone.

117
00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.030
Okay, okay.

118
00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:34.850
Because best to hear it in her words.

119
00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:35.290
Okay.

120
00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.350
Well, we'll put a link in our stories.

121
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:37.970
Definitely.

122
00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:44.150
You know, the recording of that set, it's called Tig Notaro Live, was nominated for a Grammy Award as well.

123
00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.350
Now, Tig has been in so many things.

124
00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.890
I mean, her resume is very, very, very long.

125
00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:56.310
But I did want to give a shout out for our Trekkie fans, because she has a recurring role on Star Trek Discovery.

126
00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.870
She plays Jet Reno over several seasons of the show.

127
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:03.710
This is the one sci-fi series I don't know.

128
00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.210
I don't know Star Trek.

129
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.450
Don't come for me, Trekkies.

130
00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.150
But I will have to check out Tig as Jet Reno.

131
00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.390
And, you know, just to throw even a little bit more love Tig's way,

132
00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.750
she has a podcaSt.

133
00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.690
It's called Don't Ask Tig.

134
00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.630
It is an advice podcaSt.

135
00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.810
Angela, you know I love advice podcasts.

136
00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:21.850
I know you do.

137
00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:26.950
You know, Chelsea Handler does a segment as part of her podcast that's an advice podcaSt.

138
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:30.110
And we were on Chelsea's podcast and got to give advice.

139
00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.090
It was so much fun.

140
00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:31.670
Yeah.

141
00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:35.290
And then we got to ask Chelsea, like, one thing we need advice on.

142
00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:39.230
You asked her about clothes to ski in or boots.

143
00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:40.110
Both.

144
00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:40.810
Oh, okay.

145
00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.010
I knew it was like ski gear.

146
00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:48.710
And I asked her how she makes her margaritas because I heard she makes a killer margarita.

147
00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:49.110
Yeah.

148
00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:52.610
Well, Tig's advice podcast is also amazing.

149
00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.590
Again, it's called Don't Ask Tig.

150
00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.230
It's very, very funny.

151
00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.490
And Tig is also very genuine.

152
00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:58.310
She is.

153
00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:01.390
I want to read one thing from her website that just tickled me.

154
00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.150
So she has a lot of live tour dates.

155
00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:08.250
If you want to see her, you can go to tignation.com.

156
00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:17.230
But on her bio page, she has an entry where she shares secret facts about herself, and she lists her past jobs.

157
00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.270
Oh, my gosh.

158
00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.650
Tig fast facts.

159
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.710
Tig fast facts.

160
00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.930
Here are some of her past jobs.

161
00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:31.870
Pizza delivery, child care, music promotion, barista, natural food store stalker, assistant at Xena Warrior Princess.

162
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:33.070
Wow.

163
00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:33.770
I know.

164
00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.830
Well, Tig, you are amazing.

165
00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:38.710
Just all-around amazing.

166
00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.290
You are amazing on The Office.

167
00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.790
We love you.

168
00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:47.950
And now I'm going to move us on to fast fact number two, guest star Georgia Engel.

169
00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.270
We have two powerhouse women guesting in this episode.

170
00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:56.090
I have to tell you, last night when I was prepping the final things for today,

171
00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.910
I went back and watched a few Mary Tyler Moore episodes.

172
00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:01.510
She's so good.

173
00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.490
First of all, that show is so good.

174
00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:03.790
Yeah.

175
00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.670
It makes me want to rewatch it, like, start to finish.

176
00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.410
But she plays Georgette.

177
00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:09.270
She's so good.

178
00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:10.710
She won an Emmy for that role.

179
00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:11.690
She should have.

180
00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.110
Yes.

181
00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.770
She also had a recurring role on Everybody Loves Raymond.

182
00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:17.410
And I love her on that.

183
00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:20.050
And she was nominated for an Emmy for that because she's amazing.

184
00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:24.430
But here's a fun fact I have to share about her because it's also about my hometown.

185
00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.050
Okay.

186
00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.410
So I think we've talked about this on the podcast before.

187
00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.750
There's this big outdoor amphitheater in St. Louis called the Muni.

188
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.570
And they do big musicals there every summer.

189
00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.670
You have talked about the Muni because Phyllis did the show with the nuns there.

190
00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:38.070
Yes.

191
00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:38.590
Nonsense.

192
00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:39.250
Yes.

193
00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:44.910
Well, St. Louis is very proud to brag that she has done five different seasons

194
00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.570
at the Muni in St. Louis doing musicals.

195
00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:49.350
We like to brag about that.

196
00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.650
You love a little St. Louis shout out.

197
00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:52.310
I do.

198
00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.230
And now we have a fan question from Karen C.

199
00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:56.430
in Newark, Delaware.

200
00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.230
How did Georgia Engel get on the show?

201
00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.610
And would love to hear Ellie's thoughts on working with her.

202
00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.130
I was so jealous that Ellie got to work with her.

203
00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.230
I know we didn't.

204
00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:10.270
I mean, there's more scenes of them, you know?

205
00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.770
It was really cut down.

206
00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:16.970
But in deleted scenes, they get to sit on a park bench and eat a pretzel, like, dipped.

207
00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.510
And it looks like mustard.

208
00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.730
And they both have mustard, like, all over their faces.

209
00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.650
And they have this, like, heart-to-heart while eating these giant pretzels.

210
00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.130
I mean, Ellie was so lucky.

211
00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:30.430
Well, I reached out to Brent Forrester, who directed this episode, and he said that it

212
00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:35.130
was Greg Daniels' idea to bring Georgia on the show, because he was a huge fan of her

213
00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.790
character on The Mary Tyler Moore Show.

214
00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:42.030
And he actually kind of felt like the character of Erin was of the same comedic tradition.

215
00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:48.010
And so it was kind of like, you know, the passing of, like, a generational comedy torch,

216
00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.030
so to speak.

217
00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:49.870
How cool.

218
00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:55.930
But I also texted with Ellie Kemper, and she said that Georgia was the absolute sweetest

219
00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.590
lady ever and a total pro, and she was totally in awe of how funny she was.

220
00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:03.190
She just loved her time working with her.

221
00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:06.470
And Georgia is going to be on another episode.

222
00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.530
So this is not our last time seeing her.

223
00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.990
Now, moving on to Fast Fact 3, we have an Office Ladies announcement.

224
00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.570
Speaking of advice podcasts.

225
00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.030
I wish we had music or something.

226
00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:18.490
I know.

227
00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.030
I was like, I was thinking, we're going to announce this today.

228
00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.150
And I'm like, I wish we had, like, a little jingle.

229
00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:23.930
I know.

230
00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.570
It feels like it needs one, right?

231
00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:25.930
All right.

232
00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.130
I'm going to do one underneath it.

233
00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:27.310
Ready?

234
00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:27.690
Okay.

235
00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.630
This is me typing, guys.

236
00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:30.390
Okay.

237
00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.470
You start talking.

238
00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.530
Well, I'm at the announcement part already.

239
00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:35.330
Click, click, click, click, click, click.

240
00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:35.850
Ding!

241
00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:40.330
Next week, we have a special episode of Office Ladies.

242
00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:42.490
It is Dear Office Ladies.

243
00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.650
Dear Office Ladies!

244
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:48.050
Remember a while back when we asked you to write in with your workplace dilemmas and we

245
00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:49.810
said we would do our best to give you advice?

246
00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:52.850
Well, next week, you're going to hear how it all turned out.

247
00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.370
And thank you guys so much for writing in.

248
00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.050
So many people wrote in hilarious stuff.

249
00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.030
It was so much fun reading the letters.

250
00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.010
I can't wait for people to hear it.

251
00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:02.650
Me either.

252
00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.530
So be on the lookout for that next week.

