00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:02.010
Did he have to give permission?

353
00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:05.190
Well, first of all, just for anyone who doesn't know,

354
00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:09.270
Chuck was a very popular television show running during this time.

355
00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.970
It was created by Josh Schwartz.

356
00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.430
It was also on NBC.

357
00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:13.590
It was.

358
00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:22.570
The plot was computer geek Chuck Bartowski opens an email that has been encoded subliminally

359
00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:27.570
with vital government secrets, triggering a massive download of critical information

360
00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:34.690
into his brain, prompting both the CIA and NSA to assign an agent to protect him so that no

361
00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:38.690
one can exploit this downloaded information in his brain.

362
00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.330
Yeah, like his old college roommate emailed it to him.

363
00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:42.650
So weird.

364
00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.890
And somehow he got all this information in his brain.

365
00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.030
Kind of a la The Matrix.

366
00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:48.330
Kind of.

367
00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:50.350
Without the spigot thing.

368
00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:54.290
You know, without the pokey thing that goes in the back of his head.

369
00:17:54.310 --> 00:17:54.590
Oh, yeah, yeah.

370
00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:55.090
You have to plug in.

371
00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.050
You're not plugged in.

372
00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.190
Right, to download it.

373
00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:58.670
This was a wireless download.

374
00:17:58.950 --> 00:17:59.010
Yeah.

375
00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:04.230
Well, when this episode aired, the series finale of Chuck had just aired.

376
00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:04.990
It was a big event.

377
00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:06.030
The whole series?

378
00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.910
The whole series had just ended.

379
00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:08.430
Oh.

380
00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:14.610
But in order to get and use this cutout of Zachary Levi, Steve Burgess said,

381
00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:18.330
we had to ask Warner Brothers because they own the character of Chuck.

382
00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:23.350
And they said yes, but we had to pay them in order to use their character.

383
00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:29.090
And then we contacted Zachary Levi to see if we could take some photos of him for our cutout.

384
00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.610
But he wasn't available.

385
00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:36.510
So Warner Brothers let us use like a publicity photo that they had for the TV show.

386
00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:42.030
And Warner Brothers said that their only stipulation was that we had to give them credit

387
00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:46.450
and we could not use Chuck in any derogatory way, which we did not.

388
00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:47.210
We did not.

