00:56:08.960 --> 00:56:09.520
it to him.

1264
00:56:10.320 --> 00:56:14.200
Then Nellie comes to check on him and he tells her, look, I know you're my boss, but I need

1265
00:56:14.200 --> 00:56:15.960
you to get the hell out of my face right now.

1266
00:56:16.080 --> 00:56:19.220
And she turns to Dwight and says, your little man is unraveling.

1267
00:56:19.360 --> 00:56:20.000
Fix it.

1268
00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:20.220
Fix it.

1269
00:56:20.820 --> 00:56:21.220
Yes.

1270
00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:26.620
Meanwhile, Erin is outside talking to an elderly lady, one of the people that Dwight made her

1271
00:56:26.620 --> 00:56:27.180
kick out.

1272
00:56:28.180 --> 00:56:28.980
Erin's apologizing.

1273
00:56:29.100 --> 00:56:30.800
She's saying, I'm sorry we had to kick you out.

1274
00:56:30.920 --> 00:56:33.180
And the elderly lady says, it's okay.

1275
00:56:33.180 --> 00:56:35.700
I'm going to go to Costco and search for handsome men.

1276
00:56:36.320 --> 00:56:36.600
Oh.

1277
00:56:36.960 --> 00:56:40.940
And Erin says, you're not married.

1278
00:56:41.060 --> 00:56:41.800
She goes, oh, I was.

1279
00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:44.220
My husband was my best friend and he passed away.

1280
00:56:44.560 --> 00:56:47.740
And Erin says, well, my best friend was my boss, Andy.

1281
00:56:47.940 --> 00:56:50.400
We dated for a while, but since then he rejected me.

1282
00:56:50.520 --> 00:56:53.180
And the older lady's like, he rejected you?

1283
00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:54.920
Forget him.

1284
00:56:55.060 --> 00:56:57.500
And she's like, yeah, I'll forget him.

1285
00:56:57.580 --> 00:56:58.740
You should forget your husband.

1286
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:00.880
And the older lady's like, well.

1287
00:57:00.880 --> 00:57:01.420
Yeah.

1288
00:57:02.200 --> 00:57:08.020
We had a fan question from Alex B in Canada who said, I'm so curious about this character

1289
00:57:08.020 --> 00:57:12.720
of the older woman because the actress Georgia Engel just doesn't look old enough to need

1290
00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:14.820
the kind of support that Erin is providing.

1291
00:57:15.100 --> 00:57:16.960
Do you have any info on this?

1292
00:57:16.960 --> 00:57:23.420
Well, I asked Steve Burgess about this and he said that Georgia was only 63 years old when

1293
00:57:23.420 --> 00:57:30.780
we shot this and we had to use makeup and wardrobe to try to make her look more fragile than she

1294
00:57:30.780 --> 00:57:31.680
was in real life.

1295
00:57:31.800 --> 00:57:33.460
She was a very vibrant woman.

1296
00:57:34.420 --> 00:57:40.600
And yeah, we kind of tried to work to make her look like she needed Erin to walk her down

1297
00:57:40.600 --> 00:57:41.060
the street.

1298
00:57:41.240 --> 00:57:42.480
We gave her the little cane.

1299
00:57:43.040 --> 00:57:45.020
She still looks youthful to me, though.

1300
00:57:45.020 --> 00:57:45.120
I know.

1301
00:57:45.260 --> 00:57:46.540
I don't think we fooled anyone.

1302
00:57:46.780 --> 00:57:48.100
Clearly, we didn't fool Alex.

1303
00:57:49.080 --> 00:57:51.380
Well, Ryan has been in the bathroom a long time.

1304
00:57:51.900 --> 00:57:56.120
Jim gets a text from him and Ryan basically said, look, I have to go home.

1305
00:57:56.200 --> 00:57:57.280
I can't do the presentation.

1306
00:57:57.640 --> 00:57:59.040
I need to see my mom.

1307
00:57:59.640 --> 00:58:02.960
So Dwight says, Jim, you have to do the presentation.

1308
00:58:03.160 --> 00:58:03.820
You have to take over.

1309
00:58:04.260 --> 00:58:05.360
And he's like, no.

1310
00:58:05.540 --> 00:58:10.320
And Dwight grabs Jim by the face and like squishes his cheeks together and is like, you

1311
00:58:10.320 --> 00:58:11.560
have to do this.

1312
00:58:12.140 --> 00:58:17.880
So it was scripted that Dwight is supposed to take off his glasses in that one moment and

1313
00:58:17.880 --> 00:58:20.000
get really face to face with Jim.

1314
00:58:20.000 --> 00:58:24.640
And it was also scripted that he hold Jim's face in his hands.

1315
00:58:25.280 --> 00:58:30.620
But Brent said that Rain seemed determined to make John Krasinski laugh while they were

1316
00:58:30.620 --> 00:58:31.420
shooting this scene.

1317
00:58:31.940 --> 00:58:37.260
And he said he did it by like caressing John's face in different takes.

1318
00:58:37.540 --> 00:58:43.440
And Brent said, in my experience, almost every time one actor has to touch another actor's

1319
00:58:43.440 --> 00:58:47.820
face, like in a tense scene, they almost always burst out laughing.

1320
00:58:48.040 --> 00:58:51.940
He said he's surprised they got even one usable take when they were shooting this scene.

1321
00:58:51.940 --> 00:58:58.660
I would even say that if you put these two guys in close proximity, like just standing

1322
00:58:58.660 --> 00:59:03.520
that close to one another being ridiculous, like, uh-uh, they're going to start laughing.

1323
00:59:04.000 --> 00:59:10.300
Jim is now having to put on Ryan's suit, and it's too short for him, and eyeliner.

1324
00:59:11.300 --> 00:59:16.880
And now he starts doing the presentation that's clearly written from Ryan's life and point

1325
00:59:16.880 --> 00:59:17.300
of view.

1326
00:59:17.400 --> 00:59:17.840
Yes.

1327
00:59:17.840 --> 00:59:19.700
I thought John did such a great job.

1328
00:59:20.060 --> 00:59:21.160
Such a good job.

1329
00:59:21.840 --> 00:59:26.720
So, you know, he's doing this speech, and then the spotlight goes out, and that goes

1330
00:59:26.720 --> 00:59:28.880
up in a new place, and you see him walk over.

1331
00:59:29.060 --> 00:59:32.440
And in doing so, he sort of accidentally steps off the stage.

1332
00:59:32.540 --> 00:59:32.640
Yeah.

1333
00:59:32.920 --> 00:59:37.360
The spotlight thing was scripted, but it was not scripted that he kind of fell off the

1334
00:59:37.360 --> 00:59:37.820
riser.

1335
00:59:37.940 --> 00:59:38.680
That was on the day.

1336
00:59:38.800 --> 00:59:39.640
I just loved that.

1337
00:59:39.840 --> 00:59:40.560
It was very funny.

1338
00:59:40.700 --> 00:59:41.640
John did it so well.

1339
00:59:41.820 --> 00:59:46.200
But, you know, in his speech, he says a couple of things about pyramids.

1340
00:59:46.440 --> 00:59:46.660
Yeah.

1341
00:59:48.260 --> 00:59:55.280
So, he says, the pyramids, the strongest shape ever constructed, a shape that fits all the

1342
00:59:55.280 --> 00:59:57.020
other shapes inside of it.

1343
00:59:57.520 --> 01:00:01.440
And he goes, I don't think that's, and Dwight goes, it's true.

1344
01:00:02.020 --> 01:00:03.200
Well, I looked it up.

1345
01:00:03.200 --> 01:00:07.620
First of all, it is true that triangles are the strongest shape.

1346
01:00:07.860 --> 01:00:13.060
I watched a whole video on it by a guy named It's Triggy.

1347
01:00:13.960 --> 01:00:17.100
And it's because they don't have any rotational forces.

1348
01:00:17.120 --> 01:00:19.140
All of their forces are axial.

1349
01:00:19.560 --> 01:00:20.140
Wow.

1350
01:00:20.360 --> 01:00:21.040
They're the strongest shape.

1351
01:00:21.260 --> 01:00:21.500
Okay.

1352
01:00:22.860 --> 01:00:28.320
And it is also true that a pyramid is a shape that can fit all other shapes inside of it.

1353
01:00:28.640 --> 01:00:33.100
And I watched a lot of videos and looked at a lot of graphs of how this is true.

1354
01:00:33.460 --> 01:00:34.480
And it's true.

1355
01:00:35.120 --> 01:00:35.440
Okay.

1356
01:00:36.160 --> 01:00:38.300
Every shape fits inside of a pyramid.

1357
01:00:38.700 --> 01:00:40.800
Once again, Dwight had it right.

1358
01:00:40.860 --> 01:00:41.400
He did.

1359
01:00:41.400 --> 01:00:46.300
Well, Jim finishes the presentation, and the crowd is loving it.

1360
01:00:46.480 --> 01:00:47.440
It went great.

1361
01:00:47.780 --> 01:00:48.180
Success.

1362
01:00:48.540 --> 01:00:48.880
Yes.

1363
01:00:49.180 --> 01:00:53.520
There was a deleted talking head that cuts to kind of backstage right after.

1364
01:00:53.880 --> 01:00:54.640
Oh, really?

1365
01:00:54.920 --> 01:00:58.700
And Jim's by himself, and he's so enjoying the moment, but he's trying to be coy.

1366
01:00:58.780 --> 01:00:59.620
And he's like, yeah, I'm not.

1367
01:00:59.700 --> 01:01:01.340
I mean, I wouldn't say I'm a performer.

1368
01:01:01.820 --> 01:01:03.120
Like, he has this whole moment.

1369
01:01:03.520 --> 01:01:04.620
It was really cute.

1370
01:01:04.620 --> 01:01:12.040
Back in the conference room, Toby is still teaching the self-defense course, and Kelly

1371
01:01:12.040 --> 01:01:13.980
is going to start attacking Toby.

1372
01:01:14.840 --> 01:01:18.460
Andy tries to separate them and gets hit in his other eye.

1373
01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:21.620
He ends this episode with two black eyes.

1374
01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:23.400
But he says, you know what?

1375
01:01:23.460 --> 01:01:25.420
It was a tough day, but I feel good.

1376
01:01:25.680 --> 01:01:28.980
He was coming to other people's defense both times.

1377
01:01:28.980 --> 01:01:30.960
He was there to protect other people.

1378
01:01:31.500 --> 01:01:34.900
Plus, he took some painkillers, drank some wine, took his pants off.

1379
01:01:34.920 --> 01:01:35.860
He feels really good.

1380
01:01:35.940 --> 01:01:38.100
He feels good about the day, ultimately.

1381
01:01:38.780 --> 01:01:44.420
And back at the Saber store, Nellie is going to tell Dwight he did a great job, and he is

1382
01:01:44.420 --> 01:01:45.920
going to get the VP position.

1383
01:01:46.720 --> 01:01:51.460
They celebrate with sort of this routine they do with one another, where Dwight starts punching

1384
01:01:51.460 --> 01:01:53.000
the air, kicking the fridge.

1385
01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:55.000
Then he fake punches Nellie's torso.

1386
01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:56.340
She's delighted.

1387
01:01:56.580 --> 01:01:58.040
That was all scripted.

1388
01:01:58.380 --> 01:01:58.840
Oh.

1389
01:01:59.160 --> 01:02:00.400
But the scene was bigger.

1390
01:02:00.960 --> 01:02:01.940
And I want to read it to you.

1391
01:02:02.100 --> 01:02:03.680
Here's how it was in the shooting draft.

1392
01:02:04.380 --> 01:02:07.300
Interior Saber store, back room, moments later.

1393
01:02:07.500 --> 01:02:08.660
Dwight and Nellie enter.

1394
01:02:08.960 --> 01:02:10.540
Spy shot through the door crack.

1395
01:02:10.860 --> 01:02:11.340
Dwight.

1396
01:02:11.640 --> 01:02:14.900
I'll be the first to admit, we could have integrated more Chuck into it.

1397
01:02:15.160 --> 01:02:15.640
Nellie.

1398
01:02:15.920 --> 01:02:16.400
Dwight.

1399
01:02:16.660 --> 01:02:17.560
Look at this.

1400
01:02:17.860 --> 01:02:22.300
She pulls the top of her blouse down to show her upper cheSt.

1401
01:02:22.860 --> 01:02:23.340
Nellie.

1402
01:02:23.660 --> 01:02:24.500
What do you see?

1403
01:02:25.020 --> 01:02:25.500
Dwight.

1404
01:02:26.320 --> 01:02:27.280
Goose pimples.

1405
01:02:27.280 --> 01:02:32.320
Nellie grabs Dwight and gives him a deep, long kiss.

1406
01:02:32.600 --> 01:02:38.200
He then fishes around in his mouth after the kiss and finds a fortune cookie-style message.

1407
01:02:38.800 --> 01:02:39.920
He reads it.

1408
01:02:40.100 --> 01:02:41.620
You're the vice president.

1409
01:02:41.880 --> 01:02:43.300
Yes, yes, yes.

1410
01:02:43.560 --> 01:02:46.220
Dwight starts punching the air, kicking the fridge.

1411
01:02:46.340 --> 01:02:48.000
Then he fake punches Nellie's torso.

1412
01:02:48.340 --> 01:02:49.380
She's delighted.

1413
01:02:50.000 --> 01:02:51.300
Nellie talking head.

1414
01:02:51.300 --> 01:02:55.180
I also had one that said, you're not the vice president.

1415
01:02:55.700 --> 01:02:57.980
She would have kissed that into his mouth, too.

1416
01:02:58.500 --> 01:03:00.840
Then Nellie finds Packer.

1417
01:03:00.960 --> 01:03:02.420
And this is what it says.

1418
01:03:02.880 --> 01:03:05.460
Interior Saber store, back room, moments later.

1419
01:03:05.600 --> 01:03:06.800
Nellie and Packer are there.

1420
01:03:07.080 --> 01:03:10.540
Nellie gives Packer a long, deep kiss and walks away.

1421
01:03:11.180 --> 01:03:12.020
Todd smiles.

1422
01:03:12.300 --> 01:03:14.660
He then notices something's in his mouth.

1423
01:03:14.920 --> 01:03:20.080
He fishes out a piece of paper and reads it and says, damn it.

1424
01:03:22.650 --> 01:03:28.290
Well, it's very interesting, this scene, because I felt like what was left, you know, we deleted

1425
01:03:28.290 --> 01:03:33.930
so much of that, what was left did have a weird kind of sexual tension to it.

1426
01:03:34.010 --> 01:03:36.470
And I kept wondering, like, where is this going?

1427
01:03:36.710 --> 01:03:43.250
Like, and I was actually really happy that it was just the good news.

1428
01:03:43.250 --> 01:03:44.050
You're the VP.

1429
01:03:44.410 --> 01:03:47.610
And that we're kind of, like, getting rid of the whole, like, are they going to hook up

1430
01:03:47.610 --> 01:03:47.950
thing.

1431
01:03:48.130 --> 01:03:48.370
Yeah.

1432
01:03:48.370 --> 01:03:48.430
Yeah.

1433
01:03:48.590 --> 01:03:53.070
It's pretty funny, though, that they both find something, like, what's in my mouth?

1434
01:03:53.230 --> 01:03:55.330
And it's like a fortune cookie message.

1435
01:03:55.750 --> 01:04:00.110
This episode is going to end with a tag of Jim spinning the Saber sign outside the store,

1436
01:04:00.150 --> 01:04:05.890
and then he looks down a couple storefronts, and he sees an amazing sign spinner.

1437
01:04:06.130 --> 01:04:07.670
Just, like, incredible spinning.

1438
01:04:07.790 --> 01:04:09.050
Oh, it's an art form.

1439
01:04:09.230 --> 01:04:09.350
Yes.

1440
01:04:09.350 --> 01:04:10.670
Like, legit art form.

1441
01:04:10.830 --> 01:04:15.030
And so Jim is going to try to do some fancy moves and ends up just kind of hitting himself

1442
01:04:15.030 --> 01:04:15.530
in the head.

1443
01:04:15.710 --> 01:04:17.410
He really hit himself in the head.

1444
01:04:17.610 --> 01:04:18.110
He really did.

1445
01:04:18.330 --> 01:04:20.190
John really hit himself in the head with that.

1446
01:04:20.950 --> 01:04:26.890
Adele from Manchester United Kingdom wanted to know how many takes was it for Jim to so

1447
01:04:26.890 --> 01:04:28.590
perfectly hit himself in the head.

1448
01:04:28.830 --> 01:04:33.210
And Adele, I don't know, but the hit in the head was not scripted.

1449
01:04:33.210 --> 01:04:38.810
It was scripted that he tried to do the leg thing, and then the sign falls on the ground,

1450
01:04:38.810 --> 01:04:40.410
so he starts dancing around it.

1451
01:04:40.530 --> 01:04:41.750
That's what was scripted.

1452
01:04:42.050 --> 01:04:46.150
But clearly, John just did this weird thing.

1453
01:04:46.210 --> 01:04:47.030
It was so funny.

1454
01:04:47.210 --> 01:04:48.010
It was so funny.

1455
01:04:48.110 --> 01:04:49.370
It looked like it was by accident.

1456
01:04:49.430 --> 01:04:52.270
It looked like he hit himself in the head, and then he was like, I'm out.

1457
01:04:52.390 --> 01:04:52.730
I'm done.

1458
01:04:53.370 --> 01:04:58.370
So this scene was actually scripted to go earlier, but they saved it and turned it into

1459
01:04:58.370 --> 01:04:58.870
a tag.

1460
01:04:58.870 --> 01:05:04.050
We had a fan question from Tyler G in Indiana who said, who was the really good sign spinner

1461
01:05:04.050 --> 01:05:04.490
at the end?

1462
01:05:04.630 --> 01:05:05.370
He's so talented.

1463
01:05:05.650 --> 01:05:07.310
How did you find him for the show?

1464
01:05:07.770 --> 01:05:13.610
Well, Steve Burgess said that the spinner was hired as a background performer through central

1465
01:05:13.610 --> 01:05:14.190
casting.

1466
01:05:14.790 --> 01:05:19.630
Steve said that Alison Jones originally looked for an actor who could spin a sign, but there

1467
01:05:19.630 --> 01:05:24.410
were no actors who could spin a sign in case we wanted this person to speak dialogue.

1468
01:05:25.110 --> 01:05:29.730
And then they looked for a stunt person who could spin a sign, nothing.

1469
01:05:30.590 --> 01:05:34.170
Finally, our ADs, our assistant directors, went to central casting.

1470
01:05:34.470 --> 01:05:36.950
That's where you cast all your background performers.

1471
01:05:37.070 --> 01:05:37.990
We've talked about that.

1472
01:05:38.130 --> 01:05:40.470
And they said, we need a sign spinner.

1473
01:05:40.770 --> 01:05:43.410
And that's something you would have put in your special skills.

1474
01:05:43.490 --> 01:05:43.830
Yes.

1475
01:05:44.010 --> 01:05:45.070
And they found one.

1476
01:05:45.510 --> 01:05:46.970
His name was Mike.

1477
01:05:47.470 --> 01:05:51.210
Steve wasn't sure of his last name, but he said, who knew?

1478
01:05:51.210 --> 01:05:56.330
Who knew that someone would have signs spinning on his resume?

1479
01:05:56.590 --> 01:05:57.250
But he did.

1480
01:05:57.430 --> 01:05:58.410
I believe it.

1481
01:05:58.670 --> 01:06:03.110
And I guess Phil Shea had both the signs made, but they did have to make some adjustments

1482
01:06:03.110 --> 01:06:08.930
to the handle for Mike because Mike was like, if you change the handle a little bit, it's

1483
01:06:08.930 --> 01:06:09.710
going to spin better.

1484
01:06:09.790 --> 01:06:09.990
Yeah.

1485
01:06:10.150 --> 01:06:11.250
I can give you some tips.

1486
01:06:11.470 --> 01:06:12.630
I can actually give you some tips.

1487
01:06:12.730 --> 01:06:13.030
Yes.

1488
01:06:13.170 --> 01:06:13.310
Yeah.

1489
01:06:13.890 --> 01:06:16.650
Well, guys, that was Test the Store.

1490
01:06:16.650 --> 01:06:21.250
Before we wrap up, I just want to let you know that a black eye can come in between one

1491
01:06:21.250 --> 01:06:22.010
to two days.

1492
01:06:22.450 --> 01:06:26.130
You do need to feed ants in an ant farm unless it's gel-based.

1493
01:06:26.370 --> 01:06:28.810
And you can still have baby shoes bronzed.

1494
01:06:28.970 --> 01:06:30.890
It runs between $100 to $185.

1495
01:06:30.890 --> 01:06:31.410
Thank you.

1496
01:06:33.150 --> 01:06:33.550
That's wonderful.

1497
01:06:33.770 --> 01:06:35.290
That's all wonderful news.

1498
01:06:35.490 --> 01:06:36.150
Oh, my gosh.

1499
01:06:36.170 --> 01:06:36.990
That was awesome.

1500
01:06:37.290 --> 01:06:42.890
Well, a big thank you to Sam and also to Ellie Kemper, Ed Helms, and Mindy Kaling for

1501
01:06:42.890 --> 01:06:44.990
helping to jog my memory on this episode.

1502
01:06:44.990 --> 01:06:48.970
And, of course, to Steve Burgess and also to director Brent Forrester.

1503
01:06:49.370 --> 01:06:51.670
Remember, everyone, Brent teaches writing classes.

1504
01:06:51.890 --> 01:06:56.350
He's a great teacher, and you can find out about them on brentforrester.com.

1505
01:06:56.590 --> 01:07:00.370
Thank you guys all so much for listening and sending in your questions and comments.

1506
01:07:00.590 --> 01:07:06.130
